# Template for config/secrets.env (which is gitignored and holds the REAL values).
# Copy this file to config/secrets.env and fill in real values, then keep that
# copy out of git. Kit source files reference these as ${KIT_SECRET:NAME}; the
# install scripts substitute the value at install time (see
# docs/mcp-and-secrets-design.md). A missing key makes install fail loudly rather
# than writing a broken or literal value.
#
# KEY=value, one per line. Example (placeholder, not a real token):
# SOME_MCP_TOKEN=replace-me
